[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read by tenant, channel and body, the reports hold
more than one problem. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 covers the parser only. The other problems stay open after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="radxhunter/mega-s01e03" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

Counted from `reports-4471.json` at render time: one id, one report (the export repeats some),
tenant and channel from the tenant directory, one-day moves from `desk-notes.json`.

## The problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant writes the day
  first. 7 April becomes 4 July. Reports come from every channel and every tenant.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint
  says, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. Only the `form` channel of booking-v3
  tenants. Fixing the parser does not fix this: the hint is wrong, not the parser.
- **`one-day`**: the date lands one day before or after, not flipped: "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto
  got Monday", "only June", "the invite arrived before I made the booking". That points at time
  zones and daylight saving, not at day/month order.

## Why intake missed it

`meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. The column "intake tagged otherwise" counts
the reports in each problem that intake filed under another name.

## Lessons

- A subject line says how a report feels, not what broke. Read the tenant and the body before you merge.
- A ticket marked known can still hold problems nobody has a fix for.

